<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.guest.passes ~ the superset: an unwrapped verb reaches the vendored CLI

`lares mempalace <verb> [<words…>]` passes any verb this door does not wrap through to the vendored mempalace CLI against the guest palace (`search`, `compress`, `sweep`, `hallways`, `<verb> --help`), whose own parser reads and refuses its words. `--help-mempalace` (or `help mempalace`) prints the vendored CLI's own command list. Bare, the door prints its own help and exits 2. The lane law: `lares mempalace` touches only the guest `~/.mempalace` comparator; `lares sense` touches only the sovereign sensorium.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ verb · words · help-mempalace

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`verb` params=`takes/word seat/1 as/<verb> ~ a vendored subverb`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`words` params=`takes/words seat/2 as/<words…> ~ the words the vendored CLI reads`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`help-mempalace` params=`~ print the vendored CLI's own top-level help`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/hand ~ runs the vendored CLI against the guest palace on this host; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

